From 9d098fe8865655858c4d6e0ec330bde4ad3739aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:28:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(pocket): pre-drilled entry - plunge down proved
 drilled holes

First slice of #1449. A 2D Pocket with links.approach.predrilled on
enters each level by a straight plunge down a hole a Drill operation
ahead of it in the same setup made, where the hole is proved: the
drill is at least the tool plus 0.1 mm clearance a side, and the prior
stock grid holds no material over the tool disc above the level (the
counted depth is the deeper of the grid and the drill point's cone).
The pass plan is re-seated on the hole so the cut leaves it by the
shortest, provable link. Every other case keeps the asked helix, ramp
or arc and names why. The flag on any other kind is refused at the
door. It rides EditOperationParams (undo/redo) and the MCP params patch.

Refs #1449

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
